This product contains no source code copied from any third-party project.
Every route, field name, request payload and response shape implemented here
was independently recovered by decompiling the official SRT Android app
(v2.0.41) and by reading pages the live SRT server renders to an authenticated
session — see docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PROGRESS.md and docs/VERIFICATION.md for the
evidence trail.

During development, two third-party open-source SRT clients were consulted
as a reference for wire-format facts that neither the decompiled app nor the
live server settled on their own — specifically the card-payment and refund
request shapes, which are absent from the decompiled app's offline bundle:

  - srtgo (lapis42) and its fork srtgo_plus (DKim / "dion"), MIT License.
  - ryanking13/SRT, MIT License — the origin srtgo itself vendored its SRT
    client from (srtgo's own README credits it under MIT), so the two are one
    source rather than two independent ones.

This use was read-only source analysis, recorded in
docs/analysis/ref-srtgo_plus.md: what was taken from those projects is facts
about a third party's HTTP protocol (endpoint paths, field names, fixed field
values, response-key names, and request sequencing) — not copyrightable
expression — and every field this library sends for card payment and refund
was independently re-implemented from that field list, not copied from either
project's source. No file, function body, class, docstring or constant table
from srtgo, srtgo_plus or ryanking13/SRT is reproduced here.

